00:53:42.768 --> 00:53:44.196
Six months ago.


00:53:44.197 --> 00:53:45.764
Right. And what kind
of cancer is it?


00:53:45.765 --> 00:53:46.664
Skin.


00:53:46.964 --> 00:53:49.102
- Where?
- Why are you doing this?


00:53:50.101 --> 00:53:51.200
Where?


00:53:51.830 --> 00:53:52.929
My back.


00:53:53.568 --> 00:53:56.325
There was a mole on my shoulder.
I should have checked it out a while ago,


00:53:56.326 --> 00:53:58.294
- but I kept putting it off.
- They've cut it out?


00:53:59.303 --> 00:54:00.802
Yeah, most of it.


00:54:01.261 --> 00:54:02.670
Chemo's taking care of the rest.


00:54:03.929 --> 00:54:05.427
What does that mean?


00:54:07.266 --> 00:54:09.634
It means
they'll get rid of it, okay?


00:54:09.893 --> 00:54:11.532
And if that doesn't work...


00:54:11.862 --> 00:54:13.260
I have other options.


00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:16.098
Not as fun as chemo,
but they work.


00:54:18.636 --> 00:54:19.665
Are you scared?


00:54:20.134 --> 00:54:21.503
Shut up.


00:54:22.432 --> 00:54:24.171
- Are you?
- No!


00:54:31.064 --> 00:54:32.063
Of...


00:54:32.333 --> 00:54:34.571
Of course, I'm fucking scared,
man. It's cancer.


00:54:37.039 --> 00:54:38.467
Well, are you gonna beat it?


00:54:38.468 --> 00:54:39.367
Yes!


00:54:43.134 --> 00:54:44.601
- Promise me?
- Yeah, I p...


00:54:44.602 --> 00:54:46.900
...I promise. I will beat it.


00:54:47.270 --> 00:54:49.498
Fuck cancer, okay?


00:54:49.508 --> 00:54:50.637
Can I keep driving now?


00:54:50.936 --> 00:54:52.305
- Please?
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:54:52.565 --> 00:54:53.474
Thank you.


00:54:58.400 --> 00:55:00.638
What's wrong? What's the matter?
What's going on? What...


00:55:02.606 --> 00:55:03.665
We're here.


00:55:03.675 --> 00:55:05.772
Oh, shit, sorry.
Yeah, that... that was close.


00:55:05.773 --> 00:55:06.901
Sorry.


00:55:06.902 --> 00:55:07.931
- Get out.
- Okay. Okay. Do you...


00:55:07.941 --> 00:55:09.569
I can... Do you want me
to stay with you?


00:55:09.570 --> 00:55:11.467
No, I want you to get out.
I have shit to do.


00:55:11.468 --> 00:55:12.367
All right.


00:55:12.937 --> 00:55:14.404
Go. I'll see you next Sunday.


00:55:14.405 --> 00:55:15.544
What about next year?


00:55:16.434 --> 00:55:17.732
What, you want some time apart?


00:55:17.742 --> 00:55:19.071
Will you still be here
next year?


00:55:19.771 --> 00:55:22.468
Yes, I will be here next year.
I'll be here in fifty years.


00:55:22.478 --> 00:55:23.677
I'm gonna live forever!


00:55:24.476 --> 00:55:25.835
Okay, now go.


00:55:25.845 --> 00:55:28.272
Fix whatever you need
to fix with your ex-wife.


00:55:28.273 --> 00:55:30.011
Okay. All right, I'll... Ex-wife?


00:55:30.671 --> 00:55:31.640
Oh.


00:55:32.609 --> 00:55:33.938
Well, that's just fucking great.


00:55:36.106 --> 00:55:37.974
Okay. Right. Come on.


00:55:40.442 --> 00:55:41.441
Fix your marriage.


00:55:42.180 --> 00:55:43.179
End this nightmare.


00:55:45.078 --> 00:55:46.636
Focus. Come on.


00:55:47.006 --> 00:55:48.174
Focus!


00:55:48.175 --> 00:55:50.971
Uh. Oh! Look!


00:55:50.972 --> 00:55:52.270
Have you got a puppy?


00:55:52.271 --> 00:55:53.470
- Yeah.
- Can I have a...


00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:54.838
can I have a little
hold of him?


00:55:54.839 --> 00:55:57.605
- Yeah.
- Hello! Hello.


00:55:57.606 --> 00:55:59.174
Look at you, big boy.


00:55:59.175 --> 00:56:00.743
What's your name, eh?
What's your?


00:56:00.744 --> 00:56:02.972
Ziggy? Hello, Ziggy.
Do you know what?


00:56:02.982 --> 00:56:04.509
Maybe I was a bit harsh
on Great Danes.


00:56:04.510 --> 00:56:06.138
This is a Great Dane,
aren't you?


00:56:06.139 --> 00:56:09.006
You are a Great Dane. Huh?


00:56:09.016 --> 00:56:10.515
This is nice.


00:56:11.274 --> 00:56:12.842
- Lovely, yeah.
- Mm.


00:56:12.843 --> 00:56:13.742
Good for you.


00:56:14.341 --> 00:56:16.379
Well, I'd... I'd put
a little kids pool here for Lulu


00:56:16.380 --> 00:56:17.807
but... but that's just me.


00:56:17.808 --> 00:56:19.307
- Thanks, I'll think about it.
- Okay.


00:56:19.317 --> 00:56:21.344
Um. If you're here to see her,
she's... she's sleeping.


00:56:21.345 --> 00:56:23.412
No, I'm here to see you.
I'm here to see you, actually.


00:56:23.413 --> 00:56:24.981
Don't tell me
you finally signed them?


00:56:24.982 --> 00:56:26.979
- Maybe. Signed what?
- The divorce papers.


00:56:26.980 --> 00:56:28.349
What? No!


00:56:29.448 --> 00:56:31.415
Are you insane? I haven't signed...


00:56:31.416 --> 00:56:33.374
...any divorce papers, and nor will I.
I love you. I still love you.


00:56:33.384 --> 00:56:34.782
Yeah? And what does Becka
think about that?


00:56:34.783 --> 00:56:36.281
- That's over, okay?
- Teddy...


00:56:36.282 --> 00:56:37.779
Come on,
it's... it's our anniversary.


00:56:37.780 --> 00:56:38.808
Did you forget?
You forgot, didn't you?


00:56:38.809 --> 00:56:39.977
- I never forget.
- Yeah, well,


00:56:39.978 --> 00:56:41.507
I've got you something.
I got you, uh,


00:56:41.517 --> 00:56:43.274
something sweet,
which is the sixth thing.


00:56:43.275 --> 00:56:44.913
Uh. It... I should have
some gum in my...


00:56:44.914 --> 00:56:46.112
in my pocket there.
Do you wanna reach in?


00:56:46.113 --> 00:56:47.081
- No!
- Get that out?


00:56:47.082 --> 00:56:48.080
- God! No! Look, Teddy...
- All right.


00:56:48.081 --> 00:56:49.150
...I don't know
what game you're playing


00:56:49.250 --> 00:56:50.977
but, like, enough, all right?
We've both moved on.


00:56:50.978 --> 00:56:52.477
I haven't. I haven't moved on.
Have you...


00:56:52.917 --> 00:56:54.444
- Have you moved on?
- I think so.


00:56:54.445 --> 00:56:56.983
What, as in you've...
as in you've met someone else, yeah?


00:56:57.982 --> 00:56:59.879
No, but I'm thinking about,
you know,


00:56:59.880 --> 00:57:01.509
- getting back out there.
- Don't get back out there.


00:57:01.519 --> 00:57:02.817
- Okay. Fine.
- It sucks out there. It's awful.


00:57:02.818 --> 00:57:04.345
- Well, I'll just never be with anyone else...
- Okay, lovely.


00:57:04.346 --> 00:57:06.114
- ...for the rest of my life.
- That... that's all I wanna hear you say.


00:57:06.115 --> 00:57:07.253
- Yeah, okay. I was joking...
- All right?


00:57:07.254 --> 00:57:08.282
- ...all right?
- No. No, don't...


00:57:08.283 --> 00:57:09.351
- Goodbye, Teddy. I will...
- Uh.


00:57:09.352 --> 00:57:11.049
...see you on your next date
with Lulu.


00:57:11.050 --> 00:57:13.118
- And sign those papers.
- I am not gonna sign any...


00:57:19.952 --> 00:57:21.480
- Teddy?
- Uh. Yeah?


00:57:21.481 --> 00:57:22.719
What the hell
are you doing here?


00:57:22.720 --> 00:57:24.947
What... what am I doing?
What are you doing here? Who are you?


00:57:24.948 --> 00:57:27.146
Listen, Leanne has made it
pretty clear she doesn't like


00:57:27.156 --> 00:57:29.812
- you showing up out of the blue like this.
- I'm sorry, man. Um. Rewind.


00:57:29.813 --> 00:57:31.751
How exactly do you know
my wife, Leanne?


00:57:31.752 --> 00:57:33.380
Oh, for God's sake.
We're not doing this again, are we?


00:57:33.390 --> 00:57:35.848
No, we... we're doing this, mate.
Whether or not I've done it before,


00:57:35.858 --> 00:57:37.147
- I cannot tell you, but...
- What is going on?


00:57:37.157 --> 00:57:38.416
Leanne, are you okay?


00:57:38.685 --> 00:57:41.951
This strange and, I'm hoping,
gay man is... is in your house


00:57:41.952 --> 00:57:43.081
for some reason. Do you need...


00:57:43.091 --> 00:57:44.389
...do you need me
to call the police?


00:57:44.390 --> 00:57:46.118
- Patrick, I'm so sorry.
- It's not your fault. Really.


00:57:46.119 --> 00:57:47.686
No, it's not your fault,
it's his fault.


00:57:47.687 --> 00:57:49.684
It's what's his name. Patrick.
It's Patrick's fault!


00:57:49.685 --> 00:57:51.483
- Who's Patrick?
- You know exactly who he is.


00:57:51.484 --> 00:57:52.982
- Cousin?
- He's my boyfriend.


00:57:52.983 --> 00:57:54.521
- Now unless you're here...
- Oh, fuck!


00:57:54.691 --> 00:57:56.463
...to sign the divorce
papers, I want you to leave.


00:57:56.488 --> 00:57:57.587
I still haven't signed them?


00:57:57.588 --> 00:57:59.217
Ha! Good. Finally.


00:57:59.227 --> 00:58:01.124
Yeah, something I'm pleased
that I keep putting off...


00:58:01.125 --> 00:58:02.353
- Teddy?
- ...till later.


00:58:02.354 --> 00:58:03.752
Please, just go.


00:58:03.753 --> 00:58:05.520
I'm not... What?
No. I am not gonna


00:58:05.521 --> 00:58:07.918
leave you alone
with fucking Patrick,


00:58:07.919 --> 00:58:09.187
whoever he is. Look at him.


00:58:09.188 --> 00:58:10.386
What... We don't know anything
about him.


00:58:10.387 --> 00:58:11.616
- I know everything about him.
- Do ya?


00:58:11.626 --> 00:58:13.553
Oh, really? Okay, name...
name... name three things


00:58:13.554 --> 00:58:15.451
that you know about Patrick.


00:58:15.452 --> 00:58:16.851
- He's a doctor.
- Of what?


00:58:16.861 --> 00:58:17.919
Of psychiatry.


00:58:17.920 --> 00:58:19.388
Easiest one. What else?


00:58:19.389 --> 00:58:20.886
He speaks
two other languages.


00:58:20.887 --> 00:58:24.523
Oh! Do you, Patrick?
Couple of languages, yeah?


00:58:24.524 --> 00:58:26.022
What you got? French?


00:58:26.023 --> 00:58:27.121
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:58:27.122 --> 00:58:28.819
Everyone speaks French.


00:58:28.820 --> 00:58:29.819
- They don't.
- Do you?


00:58:29.829 --> 00:58:30.987
I can get by.


00:58:30.988 --> 00:58:33.025
What, like, what's
the other one? Something basic...


00:58:33.026 --> 00:58:34.325
- Hungarian.
- Hungarian?


00:58:35.224 --> 00:58:37.961
Fair enough. Yeah. It's... Well,
that's quite... that's quite impressive.


00:58:37.962 --> 00:58:39.720
- Thank you.
- And he qualified for the Olympics in...


00:58:39.730 --> 00:58:41.658
Yeah, all right. Okay, fine.
Thank you very much. That's three.


00:58:41.659 --> 00:58:43.056
Yeah. I'm counting
the languages as one each.


00:58:43.057 --> 00:58:45.294
I don't trust him, Leanne.
Look at him. Look at his beard.


00:58:45.295 --> 00:58:46.693
Oh, for God's sake, grow up.


00:58:46.694 --> 00:58:47.962
- Grow up?
- Yeah.


00:58:47.963 --> 00:58:50.859
Want me to grow up?
Okay, I will.


00:58:50.860 --> 00:58:53.327
In a few minutes from now,
that is exactly what I'm gonna do.


00:58:53.328 --> 00:58:56.924
Then again after that, then again,
then again... then again, then again!


00:58:56.925 --> 00:58:59.762
So, don't tell me to grow up,
'cause no one grows up quicker than me!


00:59:01.461 --> 00:59:02.928
Do you want me
to call the police?


00:59:02.929 --> 00:59:04.128
- It's all right.
- I'm happy to.


00:59:04.398 --> 00:59:05.656
Hey, come here.


00:59:05.657 --> 00:59:07.096
- Don't you...
- What about you grow up! What?


00:59:07.266 --> 00:59:09.463
- Don't you want me to be happy?
- That's all I want! That's all I want!


00:59:09.464 --> 00:59:11.161
Then move on.
Patrick's a good guy.


00:59:11.162 --> 00:59:12.531
- You said so yourself.
- I would never say that!


00:59:12.861 --> 00:59:15.397
Okay, it's taken me a long time,
but I finally feel like


00:59:15.398 --> 00:59:17.656
I've got a life again. You know,
my book sales are great...


00:59:17.666 --> 00:59:19.294
Book... Book... Book sales?


00:59:19.295 --> 00:59:20.862
Yeah, and they're paying me
to write two more.


00:59:20.863 --> 00:59:22.031
You have finally
finished a book?


00:59:22.032 --> 00:59:23.391
- Yeah!
- That is phenomenal.


00:59:23.401 --> 00:59:25.128
I mean, you struggled
for so long to come up


00:59:25.129 --> 00:59:27.058
with an idea. Like, what's it...
what's it about?


00:59:27.068 --> 00:59:28.795
- You said you read it.
- O... obviously, I've read it,


00:59:28.796 --> 00:59:30.863
but what's it like...
How would you describe it in your words?


00:59:30.864 --> 00:59:32.093
They're all my words.
I wrote it.


00:59:32.603 --> 00:59:34.500
If I was to tell someone to read it who
hasn't read it then how would I describe it?


00:59:34.501 --> 00:59:35.499
- I would say...
- Fucking hell!


00:59:35.500 --> 00:59:37.028
...it's about a woman
who falls in love


00:59:37.029 --> 00:59:38.526
with what seems like
the perfect guy


00:59:38.527 --> 00:59:41.064
but then it turns out he's actually
her subconscious in human form


00:59:41.065 --> 00:59:42.804
and then he...
he kidnaps her and...


00:59:43.163 --> 00:59:44.662
- Yada, yada, yada.
- So good.


00:59:44.962 --> 00:59:46.960
- Thanks.
- That is good.


00:59:46.970 --> 00:59:48.498
And really original. Brilliant.


00:59:48.798 --> 00:59:49.697
Thank you.


00:59:50.197 --> 00:59:51.236
Proud of you.


00:59:51.765 --> 00:59:52.964
- Thanks.
- Really...


00:59:54.163 --> 00:59:55.132
Where's your ring?


00:59:57.031 --> 00:59:58.099
Uh.


00:59:58.100 --> 00:59:59.268
- Oh, shit.
- What... You... You...


00:59:59.269 --> 01:00:00.468
- your wedding ring?
- I'm sorry.


01:00:00.767 --> 01:00:03.305
Teddy, I'm really sorry.
I've been meaning to tell you but...


01:00:03.735 --> 01:00:04.963
Please don't be mad, okay?


01:00:04.964 --> 01:00:06.901
- We went to beach.
- Hmm.


01:00:06.902 --> 01:00:09.130
I went into the water with it
on and when I came out, it...


01:00:10.998 --> 01:00:12.566
I spent hours looking for it,
Teddy.


01:00:12.567 --> 01:00:13.966
I'm really sorry. I just...


01:00:14.235 --> 01:00:16.302
- I didn't know how to tell you.
- It was one of a kind.


01:00:16.303 --> 01:00:17.901
- I know.
- You know, my dad made that ring


01:00:17.902 --> 01:00:19.970
- for my... for my mother.
- I know. Hey, look...


01:00:21.399 --> 01:00:23.807
I don't know,
may... maybe it's a sign.


01:00:25.565 --> 01:00:26.704
Of what?


01:00:28.103 --> 01:00:29.142
You know what.


01:00:32.139 --> 01:00:33.008
Okay.


01:00:34.207 --> 01:00:35.465
- Fine.
- I've got copies inside.


01:00:35.466 --> 01:00:37.404
All right, I'll sign them.


01:00:41.501 --> 01:00:42.969
- You okay?
- Yeah.


01:00:50.742 --> 01:00:52.071
- So, Pat.
- Patrick.


01:00:52.401 --> 01:00:53.869
You're a psychiatrist, yeah?


01:00:53.870 --> 01:00:55.039
Easiest one, that's right.


01:00:55.468 --> 01:00:57.136
Can I ask your opinion
on something


01:00:57.137 --> 01:00:59.205
- as a... a medical professional?
- Sure.


01:01:00.603 --> 01:01:01.801
Friend of mine, right?


01:01:01.802 --> 01:01:04.100
He's, kind of, going through
a bit... a bit of a crisis.


01:01:04.110 --> 01:01:05.309
- Is he?
- Yeah, and he, sort of,


01:01:05.539 --> 01:01:08.375
feels like life is moving too fast,
faster than he can keep up with.


01:01:08.376 --> 01:01:09.774
Your friend feels this, does he?


01:01:09.775 --> 01:01:11.802
Yeah, my friend,
and he feels like one minute


01:01:11.803 --> 01:01:14.170
he was young, right?
That's how it feels to my friend, yes?


01:01:14.171 --> 01:01:15.739
And then he's blinked
and then suddenly,


01:01:15.740 --> 01:01:18.037
there's more of life behind him
than there is in front of him


01:01:18.038 --> 01:01:19.905
and he, sort of, feels like
all the... all the...


01:01:19.906 --> 01:01:21.344
- Okay.
- All the things that he had


01:01:21.345 --> 01:01:23.203
to look forward
to have been... have... have been,


01:01:23.213 --> 01:01:25.501
- and they've gone. And he...
- he really feels...


01:01:25.511 --> 01:01:27.180
...Patrick, like he's...


01:01:27.409 --> 01:01:30.277
...like he's having a nervous... like
he's having a nervous breakdown.


01:01:30.576 --> 01:01:32.874
Jesus Christ.


01:01:34.643 --> 01:01:36.871
Um. Hey, it's okay.


01:01:36.881 --> 01:01:38.179
Hey.


01:01:38.180 --> 01:01:40.508
Teddy, hey.


01:01:41.007 --> 01:01:42.944
Hey. You know, there's
an old Hungarian proverb.


01:01:42.945 --> 01:01:44.343
It goes,


01:01:44.344 --> 01:01:46.611
- "Aki kit nyulat hajt egyet Se ver."
- It's beautiful, man.


01:01:46.612 --> 01:01:48.509
No. I haven't... Nope.
I haven't translated it yet.


01:01:48.510 --> 01:01:50.478
- You've gotta calm down, mate.
- Okay. Okay.


01:01:50.479 --> 01:01:51.607
- Okay.
- Shh.


01:01:51.608 --> 01:01:53.045
Go on. Go on, then.


01:01:53.046 --> 01:01:55.474
It essentially means,
"Grasp all, lose all."


01:01:56.743 --> 01:01:58.211
The tighter you hold
onto something,


01:01:58.212 --> 01:01:59.351
the sooner it's gone.


01:01:59.810 --> 01:02:01.139
Look, I know you love Leanne.


01:02:01.149 --> 01:02:02.647
I love her more than anything.


01:02:02.648 --> 01:02:05.345
- And I know you love Tallulah.
- We're not as close but yeah, sure.


01:02:05.675 --> 01:02:07.873
Okay, but if you love Leanne,


01:02:07.883 --> 01:02:09.881
you've got to let her
live her life, mate.


01:02:10.211 --> 01:02:11.210
Yeah?


01:02:11.779 --> 01:02:14.147
- And as for your friend...
- Hmm.


01:02:15.576 --> 01:02:17.644
...well, maybe all he needs
is a change of perspective.


01:02:18.683 --> 01:02:21.650
Because sure, on one hand,
life is short.


01:02:22.580 --> 01:02:24.077
But on the other hand,


01:02:24.078 --> 01:02:26.586
it's the longest thing
you will ever do.


01:02:28.484 --> 01:02:30.183
Oh, fucking hell!


01:02:32.211 --> 01:02:34.478
- Why is he crying?
- I have absolutely no idea.


01:02:34.479 --> 01:02:35.878
I... I really don't.


01:02:37.486 --> 01:02:39.185
- Is that the papers you wanted?
- Yeah.


01:02:39.414 --> 01:02:40.783
Okay.


01:02:52.852 --> 01:02:54.381
Well, happy anniversary.


01:02:55.050 --> 01:02:56.519
There you go.


01:02:59.716 --> 01:03:01.145
Thanks.


01:03:04.682 --> 01:03:05.851
Oh.


01:03:06.220 --> 01:03:09.018
Look at Ziggy. He's grown.


01:03:09.318 --> 01:03:10.716
Do you mind
if I take him for a walk?


01:03:11.256 --> 01:03:12.215
Yeah, sure.


01:03:14.323 --> 01:03:15.582
Come on there, Ziggy.


01:03:27.251 --> 01:03:28.750
I feel like you're the only one


01:03:29.489 --> 01:03:31.318
who knows how I feel
because, uh...


01:03:32.427 --> 01:03:34.254
a dog year is
seven years, right?


01:03:34.255 --> 01:03:37.052
So that means you're living life
seven times faster


01:03:37.053 --> 01:03:39.890
- than anyone else and I'm...
- I'm living life, like...


01:03:40.689 --> 01:03:43.816
...fifty thousand times faster
than anyone else, so actually,


01:03:43.826 --> 01:03:45.795
you don't know
how lucky you are.


01:03:48.692 --> 01:03:49.961
Do you wanna have a run?


01:03:52.589 --> 01:03:54.187
Here. Here.


01:04:07.895 --> 01:04:10.393
Oh, great. Here we go again.


01:04:13.789 --> 01:04:15.028
What the living...


01:04:15.428 --> 01:04:18.224
A full beard. Yeah, of course.
Of course, I've got a full beard, yeah.


01:04:18.225 --> 01:04:19.424
That's where I am now.


01:04:21.023 --> 01:04:22.961
Fucking <i>Castaway.</i>


01:04:28.027 --> 01:04:29.994
Is that a fucking chocolate bar
on a dog beach?


01:04:29.995 --> 01:04:32.832
I mean, people are animals,
honestly. Chocolate kills dogs!


01:04:34.261 --> 01:04:35.200
Kills em!


01:04:36.499 --> 01:04:37.998
What's wrong with people,
honestly?


01:04:40.166 --> 01:04:41.295
Kills em.


01:04:43.533 --> 01:04:44.532
"Contains peanuts"?


01:04:51.226 --> 01:04:52.465
I mean, I might as well.


01:04:56.161 --> 01:04:58.000
Only a matter of time now,
isn't it, so...


01:05:12.567 --> 01:05:14.065
- What's the matter?
- Huh?


01:05:16.833 --> 01:05:17.732
Nothing.


01:05:22.268 --> 01:05:23.326
All right?


01:05:23.327 --> 01:05:25.325
- Are you sad?
- Am I sad? No, I'm not...


01:05:25.335 --> 01:05:27.662
I mean, y... yeah,
I am a little bit actually,


01:05:27.663 --> 01:05:29.132
not that it's any
of your business.


01:05:29.701 --> 01:05:30.600
Why?


01:05:31.230 --> 01:05:34.397
Why am I sad? Well, I'm sad
because life sucks. That's why.


01:05:34.866 --> 01:05:36.435
- Why?
- I don't know, it just does.


01:05:37.864 --> 01:05:40.400
- Are you angry with me?
- Am I angry with you?


01:05:40.401 --> 01:05:42.929
I... I don't... I mean, why would...
why would I be angry with you?


01:05:42.939 --> 01:05:45.336
I've never even... never even met...
Where's your parents?


01:05:45.337 --> 01:05:47.395
Mummy's shopping.
It's Daddy's day.


01:05:47.405 --> 01:05:50.163
All right, no offence, kid, but your
dad sounds like a bit of a deadbeat.


01:05:50.173 --> 01:05:51.700
I mean, leaving you alone
on a beach.


01:05:51.701 --> 01:05:53.000
Where... where is he?


01:05:57.236 --> 01:05:58.235
Tallulah?


01:06:00.174 --> 01:06:01.333
Wow, look at you.


01:06:03.001 --> 01:06:03.900
Gosh.


01:06:04.700 --> 01:06:05.699
You've gotten big.


01:06:06.038 --> 01:06:07.736
- No, I haven't.
- You have.


01:06:07.737 --> 01:06:10.404
You used to be like this big, right?
And now you're like this big.


01:06:10.874 --> 01:06:13.371
That's impossible.


01:06:13.372 --> 01:06:15.200
I know. You would think so.


01:06:20.136 --> 01:06:21.405
I see your mother in you.


01:06:22.334 --> 01:06:23.573
You're both so beautiful.


01:06:23.842 --> 01:06:26.040
Mummy says
that I have your eyes.


01:06:26.440 --> 01:06:28.567
That your eyes are
the most beautiful eyes


01:06:28.568 --> 01:06:30.876
- in the whole wide world.
- Did she say that?


01:06:31.805 --> 01:06:32.704
Really?


01:06:34.573 --> 01:06:35.842
How old are you now?


01:06:36.241 --> 01:06:37.740
- Eight, almost.
- Are you?


01:06:38.809 --> 01:06:39.808
Time flies.


01:06:42.136 --> 01:06:44.004
- How old are you, Daddy?
- I'm...


01:06:44.903 --> 01:06:46.242
Wow, I don't even know anymore.


01:06:48.041 --> 01:06:49.839
- Are you old?
- Yeah.


01:06:50.278 --> 01:06:51.436
Yeah, I'm old.


01:06:51.437 --> 01:06:53.105
- Am I old?
- Nah, you're not old.


01:06:53.106 --> 01:06:54.174
You're young.


01:06:54.175 --> 01:06:55.573
Which is the most
wonderful thing


01:06:55.574 --> 01:06:57.241
in the entire world,
let me tell you.


01:06:57.242 --> 01:06:59.041
It just goes past
too quickly. So...


01:06:59.810 --> 01:07:02.307
I want you to, uh, I want you to
promise me something, all right?


01:07:02.308 --> 01:07:04.275
Just in case I don't see you
again for a while.


01:07:04.276 --> 01:07:06.073
I want you,
all right listen to me,


01:07:06.074 --> 01:07:08.042
to do anything you want
in your life, right?


01:07:08.512 --> 01:07:11.209
So, if you wanna be, uh,
an astronaut.


01:07:11.210 --> 01:07:13.007
Or the Prime Minister
or an actress...


01:07:13.008 --> 01:07:14.836
- I wanna be a unicorn.
- You wanna be a unicorn?


01:07:14.846 --> 01:07:16.745
All right, fantastic. Do it.
Live your truth.


01:07:17.074 --> 01:07:19.182
Do everything and anything
that you want.


01:07:20.212 --> 01:07:24.278
But just don't waste
a second of it, okay?


01:07:25.377 --> 01:07:26.805
Now you can promise.


01:07:26.806 --> 01:07:28.573
- I promise.
- All right, great.


01:07:28.574 --> 01:07:30.741
I need to pee.


01:07:30.742 --> 01:07:31.941
- Do ya?
- Yeah.


01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:34.648
All right then, well,
let me get you home.


01:07:34.649 --> 01:07:35.976
Do you wanna hear
something funny?


01:07:35.977 --> 01:07:37.446
- Yeah.
- I haven't peed...


01:07:37.846 --> 01:07:40.712
for, like, eight years.


01:07:40.713 --> 01:07:42.241
That's impossible.


01:07:42.242 --> 01:07:44.180
I know. You would think so.


01:07:52.413 --> 01:07:54.809
I'm gonna get this. I'm gonna get him...


01:07:54.810 --> 01:07:57.077
...a saddle,
so you can ride him.


01:07:57.078 --> 01:07:58.277
Like the Queen.


01:07:58.377 --> 01:08:00.544
Do you think that's possible?
Go on, then. He... he's off.


01:08:00.545 --> 01:08:02.183
- Yeah.
- You could be riding him right now.


01:08:02.184 --> 01:08:04.582
- You're funny.
- Oh, really?


01:08:05.780 --> 01:08:07.378
What's the funniest thing
I've ever said?


01:08:07.379 --> 01:08:08.517
Uh.


01:08:08.518 --> 01:08:10.146
When you said
that mashed potato


01:08:10.147 --> 01:08:11.985
was ghost poop.


01:08:12.255 --> 01:08:13.953
I suppose you had to be there.


01:08:15.382 --> 01:08:16.721
Can I ask you something, Lulu?


01:08:18.519 --> 01:08:19.848
Am I a good dad?


01:08:20.178 --> 01:08:21.886
- Yep.
- Really?


01:08:22.386 --> 01:08:24.743
Come on, I can take a little
bit of constructive criticism.


01:08:24.753 --> 01:08:26.880
How could I improve?
What do you think?


01:08:26.881 --> 01:08:28.210
Mm.


01:08:28.220 --> 01:08:30.188
- More ice cream.
- Fine. Easy.


01:08:30.548 --> 01:08:32.456
As much as you want,
whenever you want it.


01:08:33.256 --> 01:08:35.353
- What else?
- Um.


01:08:35.354 --> 01:08:37.251
- More Poony-choos.
- More Poony-choos?


01:08:37.252 --> 01:08:38.850
I don't know
what Poony-choos are,


01:08:38.851 --> 01:08:41.517
but I'm presuming they're some
sort of futuristic toy thing.


01:08:41.518 --> 01:08:43.357
Sure! You can have 'em.


01:08:44.216 --> 01:08:46.383
This is easy.
Come on, what else?


01:08:46.384 --> 01:08:48.992
Um. More time.


01:08:51.220 --> 01:08:52.447
More time?


01:08:52.448 --> 01:08:53.716
More time with you.


01:08:53.717 --> 01:08:55.716
I don't get to see you
a lot of the time.


01:08:56.025 --> 01:08:57.254
You're so busy.


01:08:57.854 --> 01:09:00.191
That is the most important one
isn't it, hmm?


01:09:01.191 --> 01:09:02.060
More time?


01:09:03.059 --> 01:09:04.686
- There she is.
- Good girl.


01:09:04.687 --> 01:09:06.516
Hi, sweetheart.
Did you have fun with Daddy?


01:09:06.526 --> 01:09:09.352
Yeah, I was making him
feel better. He was sad.


01:09:09.353 --> 01:09:10.582
- Oh.
- Oi, don't...


01:09:10.592 --> 01:09:11.820
don't listen to her.
She's drunk...


01:09:11.821 --> 01:09:12.950
- All right. Okay.
- ...again, all right?


01:09:12.960 --> 01:09:14.158
Go inside.
Get ready for afternoon tea.


01:09:14.159 --> 01:09:15.357
Can I play
with my Poony-choos...


01:09:15.358 --> 01:09:16.717
- No!
- ...before I get ready?


01:09:16.727 --> 01:09:18.584
Lulu, no. You know what happened
last time. No more.


01:09:18.585 --> 01:09:20.023
Those things,
they just drive me crazy.


01:09:20.024 --> 01:09:21.591
What are they?
What... what are P... poony-choos?


01:09:21.592 --> 01:09:23.120
Bye, Daddy.


01:09:23.121 --> 01:09:24.618
Oh, no, listen babe,
before you go.


01:09:24.619 --> 01:09:27.286
Um. I know we don't know
each other very well


01:09:27.287 --> 01:09:29.624
and I don't know if I say this
often or not,


01:09:29.625 --> 01:09:31.553
I don't know
but I love you, okay?


01:09:31.853 --> 01:09:34.220
- I love you too, Daddy.
- Really? I love ya.


01:09:34.221 --> 01:09:35.858
- I love you.
- Come here.


01:09:35.859 --> 01:09:38.427
Good girl.


01:09:39.726 --> 01:09:40.895
Good girl. All right.


01:09:43.892 --> 01:09:45.320
- Hell of a kid.
- Yeah, I know.


01:09:45.321 --> 01:09:47.158
Do you know what she wants to be
when she's older?


01:09:47.159 --> 01:09:48.218
- A unicorn, I know.
- Yep.


01:09:48.228 --> 01:09:49.226
Do you know what?


01:09:49.227 --> 01:09:50.656
She might just pull it off.
You never know.


01:09:53.024 --> 01:09:54.892
- Why are you sad?
- What?


01:09:55.362 --> 01:09:57.090
It doesn't... doesn't matter.


01:09:59.458 --> 01:10:01.456
Look at you.
I mean, you're unreal.


01:10:01.756 --> 01:10:03.194
How can... Look at...
You don't age!


01:10:03.195 --> 01:10:04.822
You got... you got a painting
in the attic?


01:10:04.823 --> 01:10:06.032
I mean, what's going on?


01:10:06.562 --> 01:10:07.989
- Huh?
- You look good.


01:10:07.990 --> 01:10:09.899
You're looking good, too.
You've lost some weight.


01:10:10.158 --> 01:10:11.357
- Have I?
- Yeah.


01:10:11.727 --> 01:10:13.525
Oh. Yeah, I suppose I have.


01:10:14.295 --> 01:10:16.162
Maybe I'm finally getting
my shit together.


01:10:16.163 --> 01:10:17.831
- Who knows, eh?
- I'm still... I'm still not sure


01:10:17.832 --> 01:10:19.890
- about this beard, though.
- What, you don't like the beard?


01:10:19.900 --> 01:10:21.528
I thought you liked beards,
'cause...


01:10:23.227 --> 01:10:24.325
Consider it gone.
I'll get rid of it.


01:10:24.326 --> 01:10:25.294
- How is old Pat...
- Right.


01:10:25.295 --> 01:10:26.663
- ...speaking of beards?
- He's fine.


01:10:26.664 --> 01:10:27.723
- Is he?
- Yeah.


01:10:27.733 --> 01:10:28.731
Just fine?


01:10:28.732 --> 01:10:29.691
- Teddy.
- What?


01:10:30.061 --> 01:10:31.628
No, I'm asking for a friend.
Come on.


01:10:31.629 --> 01:10:34.725
All right, well, if you must
know, we're having some problems.


01:10:34.726 --> 01:10:36.625
Having a few problems.
Very sorry to hear that.


01:10:36.635 --> 01:10:37.763
- Yeah, I bet.
- I am.


01:10:37.764 --> 01:10:39.292
I was really rooting
for you guys.


01:10:39.302 --> 01:10:40.560
- I'm going now. Okay.
- Look at me.


01:10:40.561 --> 01:10:42.369
Look... look at me in the eye.
I'm telling the truth.


01:10:43.628 --> 01:10:45.926
The most beautiful eyes
in the whole wide world.


01:10:47.994 --> 01:10:50.033
- Goodbye, Teddy.
- See ya, Leanne.


01:10:59.294 --> 01:11:00.403
Oh, wait a second. Leanne!


01:11:03.400 --> 01:11:05.599
Leanne! Happy anniversary.


01:11:08.536 --> 01:11:09.535
Leanne.


01:11:15.599 --> 01:11:19.266
Leanne?


01:11:24.132 --> 01:11:26.530
Glasses? You... you think after
all the shit I've been through,


01:11:26.540 --> 01:11:28.068
I'm worried about glasses?
Please.


01:11:28.738 --> 01:11:29.737
Whatever.


01:11:37.370 --> 01:11:38.369
Leanne!


01:11:42.905 --> 01:11:44.404
Well, what now? I mean, what...


01:11:46.542 --> 01:11:47.471
Call Sam.


01:11:50.638 --> 01:11:51.737
What the fuck is that?


01:11:52.276 --> 01:11:53.276
That is rid...


01:11:55.034 --> 01:11:57.401
How do I unlock this thing?


01:11:57.402 --> 01:11:59.310
Okay. Fair enough.


01:11:59.910 --> 01:12:00.909
Call Sam.


01:12:01.408 --> 01:12:03.236
<i>We're sorry,</i>


01:12:03.237 --> 01:12:05.304
<i>the number you have called
has been disconnected.</i>


01:12:05.305 --> 01:12:06.672
<i>Please, check...</i>


01:12:06.673 --> 01:12:07.673
Call Sam.


01:12:07.972 --> 01:12:09.940
Don't you fucking dare.


01:12:09.941 --> 01:12:11.169
<i>...the number you have</i>


01:12:11.409 --> 01:12:13.477
Call. Call Sam.


01:12:14.207 --> 01:12:16.235
<i>We're sorry,</i>


01:12:16.245 --> 01:12:18.172
<i>the number you have called
has been disconnected.</i>


01:12:18.173 --> 01:12:20.441
<i>Please check the number
before calling again.</i>


01:13:05.610 --> 01:13:06.879
You said fifty more years.


01:13:09.647 --> 01:13:11.644
I said to you, "Will you still
be here next year?"


01:13:11.645 --> 01:13:13.773
And you said, "Yeah,
I'll be here for fifty more years."


01:13:13.783 --> 01:13:16.381
So, why would you say something
like that if it wasn't true? Huh?


01:13:21.446 --> 01:13:22.445
Fuck, Sam!


01:13:26.751 --> 01:13:28.780
I didn't even get to say
goodbye to you. I mean, I...


01:13:30.178 --> 01:13:31.676
I don't know, maybe I did.
I don't know.


01:13:31.677 --> 01:13:33.885
I've been so wrapped up
in my own fucking shit that I...


01:13:37.652 --> 01:13:39.849
Just wish I could spend
another year with you, you know?


01:13:39.850 --> 01:13:41.548
Another... Another day.
Another...


01:13:44.046 --> 01:13:45.185
few minutes. I mean...


01:13:51.219 --> 01:13:52.548
Don't worry, I'm here now.


01:13:54.546 --> 01:13:56.114
And I'm just gonna
wait for you, okay?


01:13:56.115 --> 01:13:57.853
Because what else
am I gonna do? So, I'll...


01:13:59.452 --> 01:14:00.481
I'll see you soon.


01:14:01.550 --> 01:14:02.719
Won't be long now, mate.


01:14:08.454 --> 01:14:10.122
There's never enough time,
is there?


01:14:10.782 --> 01:14:13.789
Uh. Well, no, actually,
not for me. No.


01:14:14.418 --> 01:14:15.847
- How's it going?
- It's okay.


01:14:15.857 --> 01:14:18.655
You know, I'm... I'm in a graveyard,
so it's not... it's not great.


01:14:19.484 --> 01:14:21.022
I find graveyards uplifting.


01:14:21.252 --> 01:14:22.950
They remind me
how precious life is.


01:14:22.951 --> 01:14:24.548
Yeah? Lovely. Good for you.


01:14:24.549 --> 01:14:25.788
You should write
a book about it.


01:14:26.617 --> 01:14:27.956
Not that I'll have time
to read it.


01:14:28.286 --> 01:14:30.924
It's good to see you again.
It's been a while.


01:14:31.583 --> 01:14:34.390
For me, anyway. I'm guessing
not so much for you.


01:14:41.624 --> 01:14:42.923
Do you know
what's happening to me?


01:14:43.382 --> 01:14:45.021
That your life's moving
too fast?


01:14:45.720 --> 01:14:47.319
That every few minutes
is another year?


01:14:48.957 --> 01:14:50.026
How do you know that?


01:14:51.585 --> 01:14:53.252
Because I gave it to you.


01:14:53.253 --> 01:14:54.622
That was my wedding present.


01:14:56.620 --> 01:14:57.619
You...


01:14:59.258 --> 01:15:02.095
You... You did this to me? How?


01:15:03.394 --> 01:15:05.522
- I don't know how it works.
- Can you make it stop, please?


01:15:05.852 --> 01:15:07.889
- I can't make it stop.
- Well, hang on, so you...


01:15:07.890 --> 01:15:09.388
so you don't know how...
how it works


01:15:09.389 --> 01:15:11.886
and you can't make it stop.
Why... Why did you do this to me?


01:15:11.887 --> 01:15:13.585
- What have I ever done to you?
- Don't you like it?


01:15:13.595 --> 01:15:15.353
No, I don't like it.
It's ruined my life!


01:15:15.354 --> 01:15:16.752
If your life's ruined...


01:15:17.152 --> 01:15:18.560
it's because you ruined it.


01:15:18.561 --> 01:15:20.288
The gift doesn't change
your life,


01:15:20.289 --> 01:15:22.386
it just lets you see it,
sped up.


01:15:22.387 --> 01:15:25.324
How can you call this a gift? This isn't
a gift. This is... this is a curse.


01:15:25.325 --> 01:15:26.893
Yeah, well,
it feels like that sometimes.


01:15:27.592 --> 01:15:29.091
How would you know, huh?


01:15:31.029 --> 01:15:33.127
Many, many years ago...


01:15:33.128 --> 01:15:34.795
Oh, God, this sounds like
it's gonna be quite a long story


01:15:34.796 --> 01:15:36.492
and to be honest,
I'm not in the mood for a long story...


01:15:36.517 --> 01:15:37.223
I was about to marry


01:15:37.224 --> 01:15:38.821
- a good man.
- You want me to follow you?


01:15:38.822 --> 01:15:40.660
Is that what's happening
right now, yeah? Yeah.


01:15:40.661 --> 01:15:41.960
- But before I got married
- Yep?


01:15:42.429 --> 01:15:43.598
I met a stranger.


01:15:44.557 --> 01:15:48.424
Someone who saw something in me
the way I saw something in you.


01:15:49.563 --> 01:15:52.030
And that stranger gave me
this gift, or this curse,


01:15:52.360 --> 01:15:53.629
whatever you wanna call it.


01:15:54.099 --> 01:15:56.926
And thanks to that gift,
I never married that man.


01:15:57.695 --> 01:15:59.294
Oh, why, did...
did you marry someone else?


01:15:59.724 --> 01:16:00.723
Well, I couldn't.


01:16:00.733 --> 01:16:02.830
- What, you never loved another man?
- Never.


01:16:02.831 --> 01:16:04.589
But... But hang on, you just said
you learnt your lesson.


01:16:04.599 --> 01:16:06.327
I mean, what's the point
of life if... if you're not gonna


01:16:06.328 --> 01:16:07.856
spend it love...
loving someone else? I mean...


01:16:07.866 --> 01:16:10.063
- I loved someone else. Deeply.
- Now, hang on, but you just


01:16:10.064 --> 01:16:11.593
- said you...
- Not a man.


01:16:12.062 --> 01:16:13.601
Oh.


01:16:13.861 --> 01:16:15.489
Sorry. I didn't mean
to assume that you...


01:16:15.499 --> 01:16:17.926
Yeah, okay. Cool, cool.
I'm all about that.


01:16:17.927 --> 01:16:18.926
- Thanks.
- Yeah.


01:16:19.336 --> 01:16:21.194
Look, I had what you have now.


01:16:22.133 --> 01:16:25.329
The opportunity to see my life,
all of it, in snapshots


01:16:25.330 --> 01:16:28.568
and I saw that I was wasting it
on a lie, so...


01:16:29.127 --> 01:16:30.396
I never married...


01:16:31.195 --> 01:16:32.733
and I fell in love
with an amazing woman


01:16:32.734 --> 01:16:34.762
and we spent
the rest of her life together.


01:16:35.631 --> 01:16:36.899
And that's why I come here.


01:16:36.900 --> 01:16:39.097
To tell her
that I am not wasting the years


01:16:39.098 --> 01:16:40.467
that she never got to have.


01:16:41.596 --> 01:16:44.462
And I've met another woman now,
who's amazing in different ways


01:16:44.463 --> 01:16:46.501
and I love her, too.


01:16:47.471 --> 01:16:50.468
Because as long as I'm up here
and not down there,


01:16:51.567 --> 01:16:53.135
I will live life
as much as I can.


01:16:53.965 --> 01:16:55.763
That's why I call it a gift.


01:16:58.031 --> 01:16:59.430
So that's why I'm here.


01:17:00.469 --> 01:17:01.767
Why are you here?


01:17:01.768 --> 01:17:03.265
Shouldn't you be out
living your life?


01:17:03.266 --> 01:17:04.405
Tick-tock, Teddy.


01:17:05.065 --> 01:17:06.632
Well, it's... it's not as easy
as that, is it?


01:17:06.633 --> 01:17:09.300
I mean, there's not... there's not
enough time to make things perfect


01:17:09.301 --> 01:17:11.229
but the harder I try
the... the worse things are.


01:17:11.239 --> 01:17:13.466
Why would you try
to make everything perfect?


01:17:13.467 --> 01:17:15.065
It's life. It's never perfect.


01:17:15.066 --> 01:17:16.874
Because that's what happens
in <i>Groundhog Day.</i>


01:17:17.773 --> 01:17:19.601
- What, the... the movie?
- Yeah.


01:17:19.602 --> 01:17:21.938
Well, it's got nothing to do with that.
I've never even seen it.


01:17:21.939 --> 01:17:24.266
What, you've never seen <i>Groundhog Day?</i>
All right, firstly,


01:17:24.267 --> 01:17:26.405
you've got to see it. It's...
It's tremendous. And... and...


01:17:26.775 --> 01:17:29.731
If... If... If that's not how you
end it, then... then what?


01:17:29.732 --> 01:17:30.309
Hmm?


01:17:30.334 --> 01:17:32.039
Oh, honey, I thought you
had more of a handle on this.


01:17:32.040 --> 01:17:33.599
No, I think I've got
a handle on this.


01:17:33.609 --> 01:17:35.936
Yeah, you're some sort of lesbian
wizard who's put a curse on me


01:17:35.937 --> 01:17:38.733
and now somehow, I'm gonna die of
old age before you do.


01:17:38.734 --> 01:17:40.303
- Why are you laughing?
- I don't know.


01:17:41.042 --> 01:17:42.041
I don't know.


01:17:43.740 --> 01:17:45.069
I'm actually pretty scared.


01:17:46.937 --> 01:17:48.335
Would you like another go round?


01:17:48.336 --> 01:17:49.605
Well, yeah,
that'd be nice. Yeah.


01:17:50.744 --> 01:17:52.772
- When I was a little girl...
- Another story, lovely.


01:17:53.571 --> 01:17:56.008
We didn't have any of this
fancy stuff they have today.


01:17:56.009 --> 01:17:58.506
No Poony-choos
or anything like that.


01:17:58.507 --> 01:18:00.235
God, what are Poony-choos?


01:18:00.245 --> 01:18:01.972
My brother and I would go
down to the park


01:18:01.973 --> 01:18:03.312
and we'd stand really far apart


01:18:03.872 --> 01:18:06.209
but stay connected by string.


01:18:06.210 --> 01:18:07.638
We could talk
to each other that way.


01:18:08.438 --> 01:18:10.036
We were so far away,
and yet it was like


01:18:10.046 --> 01:18:11.845
we could cross
this great distance


01:18:12.244 --> 01:18:14.043
with that string.


01:18:14.812 --> 01:18:17.240
Travel to a different time
and place.


01:18:18.279 --> 01:18:20.406
Sounds like
what you want to do, right?


01:18:20.407 --> 01:18:22.445
- Something like that, yeah.
- Hold that for me.


01:18:28.310 --> 01:18:29.648
Can you pop it in for me?


01:18:33.475 --> 01:18:35.043
And on either end
of that string,


01:18:35.044 --> 01:18:36.942
do you know
what we would talk into?


01:18:37.441 --> 01:18:38.441
No.


01:18:39.250 --> 01:18:40.279
A tin can.


01:19:19.813 --> 01:19:21.910
- Teddy, Lulu's at school if you...
- Hiya. Can I come in?


01:19:21.911 --> 01:19:23.749
- Can I come in quickly?
- Uh. Yeah. What's wrong?


01:19:23.750 --> 01:19:25.817
Uh. Do you remember, um, do you remember...
do you remember all that stuff


01:19:25.818 --> 01:19:28.045
from the wedding that we got that we
didn't use or... or like or whatever,


01:19:28.046 --> 01:19:29.743
have you... have you...
have you still got that?


01:19:29.744 --> 01:19:31.352
- Yeah, I think so.
- Great.


01:19:31.353 --> 01:19:33.350
- Why? What are you looking for?
- Can I have a look?


01:19:33.351 --> 01:19:35.010
Um. Look, I'll...
I'll know when I find it.


01:19:35.020 --> 01:19:36.917
But don't worry,
I won't be here long, all right?


01:19:36.918 --> 01:19:38.586
I'll leave you
and Patrick to it soon enough.


01:19:39.246 --> 01:19:42.213
Uh. Actually, um,
I've been meaning to tell you.


01:19:42.783 --> 01:19:44.581
Uh. Patrick and I broke up.


01:19:45.690 --> 01:19:46.849
- Really?
- Yeah.


01:19:48.118 --> 01:19:49.317
Why? What happened?


01:19:49.916 --> 01:19:52.953
Uh. He, uh...


01:19:53.353 --> 01:19:55.820
Please don't read anything
into this but...


01:19:55.821 --> 01:19:57.618
- Go on.
- Um...


01:19:57.619 --> 01:20:00.357
He thought
I was still in love with you.


01:20:01.616 --> 01:20:02.625
Did he?


01:20:05.482 --> 01:20:07.120
Fucking hell,
a lot of memories in here.


01:20:07.121 --> 01:20:08.759
Yeah. Good and bad.


01:20:09.588 --> 01:20:11.256
All right, well,
tell me about the good.


01:20:11.257 --> 01:20:13.254
I mean, I've been...
I've been so focused on the bad


01:20:13.255 --> 01:20:15.452
that I've never... I've never
actually asked you about the good.


01:20:15.453 --> 01:20:18.250
Like what... what are your
best memories of our marriage?


01:20:18.251 --> 01:20:20.149
God, that feels like
a really long time ago.


01:20:20.159 --> 01:20:22.757
Leanne, come on, come on,
humor me. Just tell me a few.


01:20:23.486 --> 01:20:25.894
- Well, like, how many is a few?
- I don't know. Like...


01:20:27.692 --> 01:20:28.751
- Ten.
- Ten?


01:20:28.991 --> 01:20:29.890
Yeah.


01:20:31.489 --> 01:20:33.117
All right. Um...


01:20:33.757 --> 01:20:38.152
Well, I always smile
when I think about how you kept


01:20:38.153 --> 01:20:40.351
apologizing to my belly
when we had sex


01:20:40.361 --> 01:20:41.589
- while I was pregnant.
- Yeah,


01:20:41.590 --> 01:20:43.057
that... that does sound
like something


01:20:43.058 --> 01:20:44.726
- I'd do.
- Yeah, yeah. And do you remember


01:20:44.727 --> 01:20:47.453
that time I finally beat you at
Scrabble and you got really angry?


01:20:47.454 --> 01:20:48.853
No. I probably let you win.


01:20:51.321 --> 01:20:53.658
Oh, I don't know,
sometimes I think


01:20:53.659 --> 01:20:56.325
about how you'd sing
to Tallulah to stop her crying,


01:20:56.326 --> 01:20:58.095
even though it, kind of,
made her cry more.


01:20:59.094 --> 01:21:00.961
Or how you'd always talk
in your sleep


01:21:00.962 --> 01:21:02.591
after you drank red wine.


01:21:03.630 --> 01:21:04.689
Oh, my God.


01:21:05.288 --> 01:21:06.756
- Uh. Oh, my God.
- What?


01:21:06.757 --> 01:21:07.955
Do you remember that...


01:21:07.956 --> 01:21:09.693
do you remember that time
you had that edible


01:21:09.694 --> 01:21:12.592
and you made me take you
to the hospital?


01:21:15.889 --> 01:21:19.125
When we fell asleep
on that train


01:21:19.126 --> 01:21:22.362
and ended up spending the night
at that motel with the bed bugs?


01:21:22.363 --> 01:21:23.532
Do you remember? And we...


01:21:24.831 --> 01:21:26.130
we slept on the floor.


01:21:27.698 --> 01:21:28.927
I loved that night.


01:21:30.695 --> 01:21:32.293
Or the time you said
you loved my soup


01:21:32.294 --> 01:21:34.332
even though I accidentally put
sunscreen in it.


01:21:36.800 --> 01:21:38.358
I miss the way
you'd kiss my eyelids


01:21:38.359 --> 01:21:39.497
when I had a headache.


01:21:41.626 --> 01:21:43.594
I miss brushing my teeth
next to you.


01:21:49.459 --> 01:21:50.627
That was only nine.


01:21:53.065 --> 01:21:54.764
I miss doing nothing with you.


01:22:04.465 --> 01:22:06.763
Did you find it?


01:22:09.101 --> 01:22:10.530
Yeah, I found it a while ago.


01:22:13.667 --> 01:22:15.894
"Do not open for ten years."
Do you remember that?


01:22:15.895 --> 01:22:17.004
- No.
- Okay.


01:22:17.303 --> 01:22:20.271
So, uh, you've got paper.


01:22:21.500 --> 01:22:22.439
Cotton.


01:22:23.268 --> 01:22:24.267
Leather.


01:22:25.906 --> 01:22:27.964
- Fruit.
- Wood. Wood.


01:22:28.463 --> 01:22:29.672
- Something sweet.
- Yeah.


01:22:30.332 --> 01:22:31.470
- Wool.
- Yeah.


01:22:31.471 --> 01:22:33.469
- Um. Bronze.
- Yep.


01:22:33.799 --> 01:22:35.137
- Pottery.
- Pottery?


01:22:35.437 --> 01:22:36.666
Do you know what this year is?


01:22:37.835 --> 01:22:39.134
I think I've got
a good idea, yeah.


01:22:40.433 --> 01:22:42.800
It's, uh, it's tin.


01:22:48.765 --> 01:22:49.774
Happy anniversary.


01:22:51.902 --> 01:22:54.140
- Is this for me?
- I think it is, yeah.


01:22:55.269 --> 01:22:56.368
You finally remembered.


01:22:57.008 --> 01:22:59.665
- Oh, what's in it?
- I don't know, you've got to open it up.


01:22:59.675 --> 01:23:01.303
Have you got a can opener?
I mean, do they


01:23:01.304 --> 01:23:03.071
- still exist? Can openers?
- Yeah.


01:23:03.072 --> 01:23:04.341
- Can opener.
- There you go.


01:23:06.139 --> 01:23:07.708
All right. Um.


01:23:22.375 --> 01:23:23.604
What? What is it?


01:23:24.303 --> 01:23:25.542
How did you do that?


01:23:30.807 --> 01:23:32.845
That's... That's impossible.


01:23:39.809 --> 01:23:40.808
How? I...


01:23:42.077 --> 01:23:43.636
- I don't understand.
- I think I do.


01:23:43.945 --> 01:23:46.443
I think I finally understand.
Why... What are we doing?


01:23:46.673 --> 01:23:47.672
What?


01:23:48.941 --> 01:23:50.110
Why aren't we together?


01:23:50.779 --> 01:23:51.978
Lots of reasons. We...


01:23:52.278 --> 01:23:54.075
- had problems.
- Yeah, sure, we had problems.


01:23:54.076 --> 01:23:56.314
But now? Like, why...
why aren't we together?


01:23:56.674 --> 01:23:57.643
Now?


01:23:58.242 --> 01:24:00.509
- It's more complicated than that, Teddy.
- It's not really. It isn't.


01:24:00.510 --> 01:24:02.279
It isn't.
I think it's very simple.


01:24:03.578 --> 01:24:04.577
I love you.


01:24:05.176 --> 01:24:06.344
- I love you...
- I love you.


01:24:06.345 --> 01:24:08.973
I love you too,
but it's not that simple, Teddy.


01:24:08.983 --> 01:24:10.012
No, listen, listen.


01:24:10.342 --> 01:24:12.579
Listen, we've always done things
backwards, haven't we, right?


01:24:12.580 --> 01:24:14.108
So, I kissed you,
and then I met you.


01:24:15.947 --> 01:24:17.515
And then that kiss
nearly killed me.


01:24:18.614 --> 01:24:21.911
But not kissing you
would have been so much worse.


01:24:22.980 --> 01:24:24.149
So, what are we waiting for?


01:24:24.709 --> 01:24:25.718
We have love.


01:24:26.347 --> 01:24:27.346
We have a history.


01:24:28.345 --> 01:24:29.245
We have a great kid.


01:24:29.544 --> 01:24:31.672
And we still have time, okay?


01:24:31.682 --> 01:24:33.511
And that time
is running out so fast.


01:24:34.550 --> 01:24:36.008
Believe me, Leanne,


01:24:36.248 --> 01:24:38.446
it is running out so fast.


01:24:43.542 --> 01:24:45.709
Every second that...
that you wait is a second


01:24:45.710 --> 01:24:47.079
that you will never get back.


01:24:48.447 --> 01:24:52.144
So how many more seconds
of this crazy, short life...


01:24:54.112 --> 01:24:55.351
are you willing to waste?


01:24:57.079 --> 01:24:58.079
I don't know.


01:24:58.988 --> 01:24:59.987
Ten?


01:25:00.546 --> 01:25:01.486
All right.


01:25:02.545 --> 01:25:03.614
Your time...


01:25:05.112 --> 01:25:06.081
starts...


01:25:07.380 --> 01:25:08.449
now.


01:25:20.119 --> 01:25:22.387
Wait. That was only nine.


01:26:24.021 --> 01:26:25.859
<i>First morning
as a married man, huh?</i>


01:26:25.860 --> 01:26:26.989
<i>How do you feel?</i>


01:26:29.856 --> 01:26:32.264
I made mimosa!


01:26:33.363 --> 01:26:35.721
Wow, you really
like mimosas, huh?


01:26:37.989 --> 01:26:38.988
Hi.


01:26:41.026 --> 01:26:43.324
- Morning.
- Where's my... where's my laptop?


01:26:44.693 --> 01:26:45.891
What are you doing?


01:26:46.661 --> 01:26:47.660
Okay, I'm gonna...


01:26:48.729 --> 01:26:51.287
Teddy, what are you doing?


01:26:51.297 --> 01:26:54.393
I am gonna just book
our honeymoon.


01:26:54.394 --> 01:26:56.261
You're kidding me.
Where are we going?


01:26:56.262 --> 01:26:58.089
- Do you care? Huh?
- No.


01:26:58.090 --> 01:26:59.528
Okay,


01:26:59.529 --> 01:27:02.496
where's my phone? There it is.
Okay, right.


01:27:02.497 --> 01:27:04.024
- Wow!
- Where is it? Where is it?


01:27:04.025 --> 01:27:05.993
B, B, B, B...


01:27:06.563 --> 01:27:08.531
Belinda, hi. Uh, it's Teddy.
Listen.


01:27:08.791 --> 01:27:10.489
Listen to me, uh, Belinda.


01:27:10.499 --> 01:27:13.126
This is gonna sound like it's really
out of the blue but I quit, okay?


01:27:13.127 --> 01:27:15.165
I quit my job because
my heart's not in it, Belinda.


01:27:15.495 --> 01:27:16.962
It never has been,
and to be honest,


01:27:16.963 --> 01:27:19.591
I'm not a hundred percent sure
or what it is I do exactly,


01:27:19.601 --> 01:27:21.390
- so there you go. I quit.
- What are you doing?


01:27:21.399 --> 01:27:22.997
- All right...
- We can't... we can't survive


01:27:22.998 --> 01:27:25.165
on just my income alone.


01:27:25.166 --> 01:27:26.794
- Yeah.
- Belinda, I don't quit,


01:27:26.795 --> 01:27:29.161
but I will be taking paid leave
immediately, all right?


01:27:29.162 --> 01:27:30.791
And no more overtime, okay?


01:27:30.801 --> 01:27:33.058
And just a heads up, I'm gonna
start studying photography


01:27:33.059 --> 01:27:34.397
because it's what I love.


01:27:34.398 --> 01:27:37.964
And Belinda, life is too short
to not do what you love doing,


01:27:37.965 --> 01:27:40.632
so there you go. As soon as
I find a job doing what I love,


01:27:41.202 --> 01:27:42.400
I quit, all right?


01:27:42.401 --> 01:27:44.498
So, if you... Call me back
when you get this message,


01:27:44.499 --> 01:27:46.796
and I hope you're well
and love to Peter and the kids.


01:27:46.797 --> 01:27:48.026
All the best. Bye.


01:27:48.035 --> 01:27:49.035
Are you insane?


01:27:50.563 --> 01:27:51.561
Not anymore.


01:27:51.562 --> 01:27:53.000
You were just
about to quit your job.


01:27:53.001 --> 01:27:55.927
Yes. So should you,
because you fucking hate your job.


01:27:55.928 --> 01:27:58.135
Yeah, and when I come up
with a good idea for a novel,


01:27:58.136 --> 01:28:00.263
- I will quit my job.
- Right, okay. How about this?


01:28:00.264 --> 01:28:03.700
Um. Right, so a woman meets
the perfect guy, right,


01:28:03.701 --> 01:28:05.369
except he's not the perfect guy.


01:28:05.370 --> 01:28:08.836
Turns out that he's actually
her subconscious in human form.


01:28:08.837 --> 01:28:11.164
Uh. And then he kidnaps her,
it becomes some sort of thriller.


01:28:11.165 --> 01:28:13.132
I don't know, I haven't read
it, but there you go.


01:28:13.133 --> 01:28:15.000
- How about that?
- Uh. That's a pretty good idea.


01:28:15.001 --> 01:28:16.640
It's yours.
No, I mean literally.


01:28:17.139 --> 01:28:18.167
- It's mine?
- Literally,


01:28:18.168 --> 01:28:19.696
it's your idea, yeah.


01:28:19.697 --> 01:28:21.834
- Okay. Um...
- What are you on this morning?


01:28:21.835 --> 01:28:23.832
Uh. Right.


01:28:23.833 --> 01:28:25.132
Please.


01:28:25.871 --> 01:28:28.468
- <i>Hey, man, what's up?</i>
- Sam! Hello.


01:28:28.469 --> 01:28:30.736
Hello, mate. It's so good
to hear your voice. It's...


01:28:30.737 --> 01:28:33.365
- <i>What?</i>
- It's Teddy. Listen to me. Uh...


01:28:33.375 --> 01:28:34.702
- <i>What?</i>
- Listen to me


01:28:34.703 --> 01:28:36.571
very fucking carefully,
all right? Okay.


01:28:36.572 --> 01:28:38.299
You... I want you
to put a reminder


01:28:38.300 --> 01:28:40.808
in your phone
for tomorrow, okay?


01:28:41.138 --> 01:28:44.504
To... To go to see a doctor
for a skin cancer screening.


01:28:44.505 --> 01:28:46.332
Do you hear me?
Skin cancer screening, right?


01:28:46.333 --> 01:28:48.471
Then I want you to put...
to put a reminder in your phone


01:28:48.701 --> 01:28:50.638
to do the same again
the next year and again


01:28:50.639 --> 01:28:52.506
and again and again.
And, mate, if you don't go,


01:28:52.507 --> 01:28:54.505
I'm gonna drag you there
myself, all right?


01:28:54.506 --> 01:28:57.572
I've just got a bad feeling.
Okay? And Sam, listen.


01:28:57.573 --> 01:28:59.271
I love you, okay?


01:28:59.641 --> 01:29:02.868
I know I... That's gonna sound
weird, uh, coming from me now


01:29:02.878 --> 01:29:05.705
but I do, I love you. And...
and I don't say it enough


01:29:05.706 --> 01:29:07.334
because none of us
say it enough, do we?


01:29:07.344 --> 01:29:09.702
- So, there you go. I love you.
- <i>I... I love you too, man.</i>


01:29:09.712 --> 01:29:12.109
Okay? Um. Oh, yeah,
one more thing.


01:29:12.110 --> 01:29:13.807
Um. If you...


01:29:13.808 --> 01:29:16.405
When you hear
of something called Poony-choos,


01:29:16.406 --> 01:29:19.202
do you hear me, Poony-choos,
invest, mate.


01:29:19.203 --> 01:29:20.841
Invest everything
you've got, okay?


01:29:20.842 --> 01:29:22.739
- You won't regret it, trust me.
- <i>Poony-choos?</i>


01:29:22.740 --> 01:29:24.807
- All right, mate.
- <i>What the fuck are Poony-choos?</i>


01:29:24.808 --> 01:29:26.976
I'll see you later, okay?
Bye-bye.


01:29:27.276 --> 01:29:29.474
Right. Uh. What else? Oh, yeah.


01:29:30.413 --> 01:29:32.640
Uh. Do you remember
my, uh, ex-girlfriend?


01:29:32.641 --> 01:29:34.570
- The one from New Year's Eve?
- Yeah, yeah,


01:29:34.580 --> 01:29:35.877
she's getting married. Becka.


01:29:35.878 --> 01:29:37.647
- Becka, yes.
- Yeah, what about her?


01:29:42.512 --> 01:29:44.481
- Remind me to give her this.
- What's that?


